#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Qiskit to implement ideas from the single-systems lesson."
msgstr "Menggunakan Qiskit untuk melaksanakan idea daripada pelajaran sistem tunggal."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan Qiskit"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we'll take a look at some Qiskit implementations of the concepts introduced in this lesson.\n"
"If you wish to run these implementations yourself, which is strongly encouraged, consult the [Install Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) page in the\n"
"[IBM Quantum Documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com) for details on how to set up Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bahagian ini, kita akan melihat beberapa pelaksanaan Qiskit bagi konsep-konsep yang diperkenalkan dalam pelajaran ini.\n"
"Jika anda ingin menjalankan pelaksanaan ini sendiri, yang sangat digalakkan, rujuk halaman [Pasang Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) dalam\n"
"[Dokumentasi IBM Quantum](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com) untuk butiran tentang cara menyediakan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It should be understood that Qiskit is under continual development, and is principally focused on maximizing the performance of the quantum computers it is used to operate, which themselves continue to evolve.\n"
"As a result, Qiskit is subject to changes that may occasionally lead to code deprecation.\n"
"With this in mind, we'll always execute the following commands prior to presenting examples of Qiskit code in this course, so that it is clear which version of Qiskit has been used.\n"
"Starting with Qiskit v1.0, this is a simple way to see what version of Qiskit is currently installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu difahami bahawa Qiskit sedang dalam pembangunan berterusan, dan memberi tumpuan utama kepada memaksimumkan prestasi komputer kuantum yang digunakannya, yang turut terus berkembang.\n"
"Akibatnya, Qiskit tertakluk kepada perubahan yang kadangkala boleh menyebabkan susutan kod.\n"
"Dengan ini dalam fikiran, kita akan sentiasa melaksanakan arahan berikut sebelum membentangkan contoh kod Qiskit dalam kursus ini, supaya jelas versi Qiskit yang telah digunakan.\n"
"Bermula dengan Qiskit v1.0, ini adalah cara mudah untuk melihat versi Qiskit yang sedang dipasang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are running this in a cloud-based Python environment, you might need to install some of the following packages:\n"
msgstr "Jika anda menjalankan ini dalam persekitaran Python berasaskan awan, anda mungkin perlu memasang beberapa pakej berikut:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vectors and matrices in Python {#vectors-and-matrices-in-python}"
msgstr "Vektor dan matriks dalam Python {#vectors-and-matrices-in-python}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit uses the Python programming language, so before discussing Qiskit specifically, it may be helpful to very briefly discuss matrix and vector computations in Python.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit menggunakan bahasa pengaturcaraan Python, jadi sebelum membincangkan Qiskit secara khusus, mungkin berguna untuk membincangkan secara ringkas pengiraan matriks dan vektor dalam Python.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In Python, matrix and vector computations can be performed using the `array` class from the `NumPy` library, which provides functionality for many numerical and scientific computations.\n"
"The following code loads this library, defines two column vectors, `ket0` and `ket1`, corresponding to the qubit state vectors $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$, and then prints their average.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam Python, pengiraan matriks dan vektor boleh dilakukan menggunakan kelas `array` daripada pustaka `NumPy`, yang menyediakan fungsi untuk banyak pengiraan berangka dan saintifik.\n"
"Kod berikut memuatkan pustaka ini, mentakrifkan dua vektor lajur, `ket0` dan `ket1`, yang sepadan dengan vektor keadaan qubit $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert 1\\rangle$, dan kemudian mencetak puratanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also use `array` to create matrices that can represent operations.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga boleh menggunakan `array` untuk mencipta matriks yang boleh mewakili operasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that all code appearing within a given lesson in this course is expected to be run sequentially.\n"
"Therefore, we don't need to import `NumPy` again here, because it has already been imported.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ambil perhatian bahawa semua kod yang muncul dalam pelajaran tertentu dalam kursus ini dijangka dijalankan secara berurutan.\n"
"Oleh itu, kita tidak perlu mengimport `NumPy` lagi di sini, kerana ia telah pun diimport.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix multiplication, including matrix-vector multiplication as a special case, can be performed using the `@` operator.\n"
msgstr "Pendaraban matriks, termasuk pendaraban matriks-vektor sebagai kes khas, boleh dilakukan menggunakan operator `@`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This output formatting leaves something to be desired, visually speaking.\n"
"One solution, for situations that demand something prettier, is to use the`array_to_latex` function in Qiskit, from the `qiskit.visualization` module.\n"
"Note that, in the code that follows, we're using Python's generic `display` function (especially in notebooks), because it can render objects using richer representations, whereas `print()` simply uses the object's string representation. This is similar to how `NumPy` arrays provide their own specialized formatting while Python lists use the default list representation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Format output ini agak kurang menarik secara visual.\n"
"Satu penyelesaian, untuk situasi yang memerlukan sesuatu yang lebih cantik, adalah dengan menggunakan fungsi `array_to_latex` dalam Qiskit, daripada modul `qiskit.visualization`.\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa, dalam kod yang berikut, kita menggunakan fungsi `display` generik Python (terutamanya dalam buku nota), kerana ia boleh merender objek menggunakan perwakilan yang lebih kaya, manakala `print()` hanya menggunakan perwakilan rentetan objek tersebut. Ini serupa dengan cara tatasusunan `NumPy` menyediakan pemformatan khusus mereka sendiri manakala senarai Python menggunakan perwakilan senarai lalai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1  \\\\\n"
" 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1  \\\\\n"
" 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & \\frac{3}{4}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & \\frac{3}{4}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "States, measurements, and operations {#states-measurements-and-operations}"
msgstr "Keadaan, pengukuran, dan operasi {#states-measurements-and-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit includes several classes that allow for states, measurements, and operations to be created and manipulated — so there is no need to program everything required to simulate quantum states, measurements, and operations in Python.\n"
"Some examples to help you to get started are included below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit merangkumi beberapa kelas yang membolehkan keadaan, pengukuran, dan operasi dicipta dan dimanipulasi — jadi tidak perlu mengaturcara semua yang diperlukan untuk mensimulasi keadaan kuantum, pengukuran, dan operasi dalam Python.\n"
"Beberapa contoh untuk membantu anda bermula disertakan di bawah.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define and display state vectors {#define-and-display-state-vectors}"
msgstr "Takrifkan dan paparkan vektor keadaan {#define-and-display-state-vectors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The`Statevector` class in Qiskit provides functionality for defining and manipulating quantum state vectors.\n"
"In the code that follows, the `Statevector` class is imported and a few vectors are defined.\n"
"(We're also importing the `sqrt` function from the `NumPy` library to compute a square root.\n"
"This function could, alternatively, be called as `np.sqrt` provided that `NumPy` has already been imported, as it has above; this is merely a different way to import and use this specific function alone.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelas `Statevector` dalam Qiskit menyediakan fungsi untuk mentakrifkan dan memanipulasi vektor keadaan kuantum.\n"
"Dalam kod yang berikut, kelas `Statevector` diimport dan beberapa vektor ditakrifkan.\n"
"(Kita juga mengimport fungsi `sqrt` daripada pustaka `NumPy` untuk mengira punca kuasa dua.\n"
"Fungsi ini boleh, secara alternatif, dipanggil sebagai `np.sqrt` dengan syarat `NumPy` telah diimport, seperti yang telah dilakukan di atas; ini hanyalah cara berbeza untuk mengimport dan menggunakan fungsi khusus ini sahaja.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Statevector` class includes a `draw` method for displaying state vectors in a variety of ways, including\n"
"`text` for plain text, `latex` for rendered LaTeX, and `latex_source` for LaTeX code, which can be handy for cutting and pasting into documents.\n"
"(Use `print` rather than `display` to show LaTeX code for best results.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelas `Statevector` merangkumi kaedah `draw` untuk memaparkan vektor keadaan dalam pelbagai cara, termasuk\n"
"`text` untuk teks biasa, `latex` untuk LaTeX yang dirender, dan `latex_source` untuk kod LaTeX, yang berguna untuk disalin dan ditampal ke dalam dokumen.\n"
"(Gunakan `print` dan bukannya `display` untuk menunjukkan kod LaTeX dengan hasil terbaik.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Statevector` class also includes the `is_valid` method, which checks to see if a given vector is a valid quantum state vector (in other words, that it has Euclidean norm equal to 1):\n"
msgstr "Kelas `Statevector` juga merangkumi kaedah `is_valid`, yang menyemak sama ada vektor yang diberikan adalah vektor keadaan kuantum yang sah (dengan kata lain, bahawa ia mempunyai norma Euklid bersamaan 1):\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulating measurements using `Statevector` {#simulating-measurements-using-statevector}"
msgstr "Mensimulasi pengukuran menggunakan `Statevector` {#simulating-measurements-using-statevector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we will see one way that measurements of quantum states can be simulated in Qiskit, using the `measure` method from the `Statevector` class.\n"
"Let's use the same qubit state vector `v` defined previously.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya kita akan melihat satu cara pengukuran keadaan kuantum boleh disimulasi dalam Qiskit, menggunakan kaedah `measure` daripada kelas `Statevector`.\n"
"Mari kita gunakan vektor keadaan qubit `v` yang sama seperti yang ditakrifkan sebelum ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2 i}{3}) |0\\rangle- \\frac{2}{3} |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2 i}{3}) |0\\rangle- \\frac{2}{3} |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Running the `measure` method simulates a standard basis measurement.\n"
"It returns the outcome of that measurement, plus the new quantum state vector of the system after the measurement.\n"
"(Here we're using Python's `print` function with an `f` prefix for formatted printing with embedded expressions.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Menjalankan kaedah `measure` mensimulasi pengukuran asas standard.\n"
"Ia mengembalikan hasil pengukuran tersebut, ditambah dengan vektor keadaan kuantum baru sistem selepas pengukuran.\n"
"(Di sini kita menggunakan fungsi `print` Python dengan awalan `f` untuk percetakan berformat dengan ungkapan terbenam.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$- |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$- |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurement outcomes are probabilistic, so this method can return different results when run multiple times.\n"
"For the particular example of the vector `v` defined above, the `measure` method defines the quantum state vector after the measurement takes place to be\n"
msgstr ""
"Hasil pengukuran adalah berkebarangkalian, jadi kaedah ini boleh mengembalikan hasil yang berbeza apabila dijalankan beberapa kali.\n"
"Untuk contoh khusus vektor `v` yang ditakrifkan di atas, kaedah `measure` mentakrifkan vektor keadaan kuantum selepas pengukuran berlaku sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{1 + 2i}{\\sqrt{5}}\\biggr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{1 + 2i}{\\sqrt{5}}\\biggr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(rather than $\\vert 0\\rangle$) or\n"
msgstr "(berbanding $\\vert 0\\rangle$) atau\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"- \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"- \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(rather than $\\vert 1\\rangle$), depending on the measurement outcome.\n"
"In both cases, the alternatives to $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$ are, in fact, equivalent to these state vectors; they are said to to *equivalent up to a global phase* because one is equal to the other multiplied by a complex number on the unit circle.\n"
"This issue is discussed in greater detail in the [Quantum circuits](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction) lesson, and can safely be ignored for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"(berbanding $\\vert 1\\rangle$), bergantung pada hasil pengukuran.\n"
"Dalam kedua-dua kes, alternatif kepada $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert 1\\rangle$ sebenarnya setara dengan vektor keadaan ini; ia dikatakan *setara sehingga fasa global* kerana satu sama dengan yang lain didarab dengan nombor kompleks pada bulatan unit.\n"
"Isu ini dibincangkan dengan lebih terperinci dalam pelajaran [Litar kuantum](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction), dan boleh diabaikan buat masa ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Statevector` will throw an error if the `measure` method is applied to an invalid quantum state vector.\n"
msgstr "`Statevector` akan melemparkan ralat jika kaedah `measure` digunakan pada vektor keadaan kuantum yang tidak sah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Statevector` also comes with a `sample_counts` method that allows for the simulation of any number of measurements on the system, each time starting with a fresh copy of the state. For example, the following code shows the outcome of measuring the vector `v` $1000$ times, which (with high probability) results in the outcome $0$ approximately $5$ out of every $9$ times (or about $556$ of the $1000$ trials) and the outcome $1$ approximately $4$ out of every $9$ times (or about $444$ out of the $1000$ trials).\n"
"The code that follows also demonstrates the `plot_histogram` function from the `qiskit.visualization` module for visualizing the results.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Statevector` juga dilengkapi dengan kaedah `sample_counts` yang membolehkan simulasi sebarang bilangan pengukuran pada sistem, setiap kali bermula dengan salinan segar keadaan tersebut. Sebagai contoh, kod berikut menunjukkan hasil pengukuran vektor `v` sebanyak $1000$ kali, yang (dengan kebarangkalian tinggi) menghasilkan hasil $0$ kira-kira $5$ daripada setiap $9$ kali (atau kira-kira $556$ daripada $1000$ percubaan) dan hasil $1$ kira-kira $4$ daripada setiap $9$ kali (atau kira-kira $444$ daripada $1000$ percubaan).\n"
"Kod yang berikut juga menunjukkan fungsi `plot_histogram` daripada modul `qiskit.visualization` untuk memvisualisasikan keputusan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/fde6ccf9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/fde6ccf9-0.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Running this code on your own multiple times, with different numbers of samples in place of $1000$, may be helpful for developing some intuition for how the number of trials influences the number of times each outcome appears.\n"
"With more and more samples, the fraction of samples for each possibility is likely to get closer and closer to the corresponding probability.\n"
"This phenomenon, more generally speaking, is known as the *law of large numbers* in probability theory.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menjalankan kod ini sendiri beberapa kali, dengan bilangan sampel yang berbeza menggantikan $1000$, mungkin berguna untuk membina intuisi tentang bagaimana bilangan percubaan mempengaruhi bilangan kali setiap hasil muncul.\n"
"Dengan lebih banyak sampel, pecahan sampel bagi setiap kemungkinan berkemungkinan semakin hampir kepada kebarangkalian yang sepadan.\n"
"Fenomena ini, secara lebih amnya, dikenali sebagai *hukum nombor besar* dalam teori kebarangkalian.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perform operations with `Operator` and `Statevector` {#perform-operations-with-operator-and-statevector}"
msgstr "Lakukan operasi dengan `Operator` dan `Statevector` {#perform-operations-with-operator-and-statevector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary operations can be defined in Qiskit using the `Operator` class, as in the example that follows.\n"
"This class includes a `draw` method with similar arguments to `Statevector`.\n"
"Note that the `latex` option produces results equivalent to `array_to_latex`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi unitari boleh ditakrifkan dalam Qiskit menggunakan kelas `Operator`, seperti dalam contoh yang berikut.\n"
"Kelas ini merangkumi kaedah `draw` dengan argumen yang serupa dengan `Statevector`.\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa pilihan `latex` menghasilkan keputusan yang setara dengan `array_to_latex`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can apply a unitary operation to a state vector using the `evolve` method.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menggunakan operasi unitari pada vektor keadaan menggunakan kaedah `evolve`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$(0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i) |0\\rangle+(-0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i) |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$(0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i) |0\\rangle+(-0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i) |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A preview of quantum circuits {#a-preview-of-quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Pratonton litar kuantum {#a-preview-of-quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits won't be formally introduced until the [Quantum circuits](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction) lesson, which is the third lesson in this course, but we can nevertheless experiment with composing qubit unitary operations using the`QuantumCircuit` class in Qiskit.\n"
"In particular, we may define a quantum circuit (which, in this case, will simply be a sequence of unitary operations performed on a single qubit) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar kuantum tidak akan diperkenalkan secara rasmi sehingga pelajaran [Litar kuantum](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction), yang merupakan pelajaran ketiga dalam kursus ini, tetapi kita tetap boleh bereksperimen dengan menggubah operasi unitari qubit menggunakan kelas `QuantumCircuit` dalam Qiskit.\n"
"Khususnya, kita boleh mentakrifkan litar kuantum (yang dalam kes ini hanya merupakan urutan operasi unitari yang dilakukan pada satu qubit) seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/68490946-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/68490946-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're using the `draw` method from the `QuantumCircuit` class with the `mpl` renderer (short for `Matplotlib`, a Python visualization library).\n"
"This is the only renderer we'll use for quantum circuits in this course, but there are other options, including a text-based and a LaTeX-based renderer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita menggunakan kaedah `draw` daripada kelas `QuantumCircuit` dengan renderer `mpl` (singkatan untuk `Matplotlib`, pustaka visualisasi Python).\n"
"Ini adalah satu-satunya renderer yang akan kita gunakan untuk litar kuantum dalam kursus ini, tetapi terdapat pilihan lain, termasuk renderer berasaskan teks dan berasaskan LaTeX.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operations are applied sequentially, starting on the left and ending on the right in the diagram.\n"
"A handy way to get the unitary matrix corresponding to this circuit is to use the `from_circuit` method from the `Operator` class.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi-operasi digunakan secara berurutan, bermula dari kiri dan berakhir di kanan dalam gambar rajah.\n"
"Cara yang berguna untuk mendapatkan matriks unitari yang sepadan dengan litar ini adalah menggunakan kaedah `from_circuit` daripada kelas `Operator`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i & 0.8535533906 + 0.3535533906 i  \\\\\n"
" -0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i & 0.3535533906 + 0.1464466094 i  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i & 0.8535533906 + 0.3535533906 i  \\\\\n"
" -0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i & 0.3535533906 + 0.1464466094 i  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also initialize a starting quantum state vector and then evolve that state according to the sequence of operations described by the circuit.\n"
